nline Learner Licence test in India?","answer":"The computerized learner test consists of 15 multiple-choice questions covering Indian road signs, traffic signals, and fundamental driving regulations. You must answer at least 11 questions correctly (60% score) within the allotted 30 seconds per question to pass.","displayOrder":0,"status":"PUBLISHED","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","sourceUrl":"https://sarathi.parivahan.gov.in"},{"question":"When can I apply for a permanent driving licence after getting my learner licence?","answer":"You can apply for a permanent driving licence after 30 days from your Learner Licence issue date. You must apply within 180 days (6 months) before the learner licence expires.","displayOrder":0,"status":"PUBLISHED","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","sourceUrl":"https://morth.nic.in"}],"rejectionReasons":[{"title":"Name or Date of Birth Mismatch on Aadhaar","description":"If the name on your 10th marksheet or birth certificate does not match the name returned by Aadhaar e-KYC, the application is halted.","solution":"Update your Aadhaar details first at an Aadhaar Seva Kendra, or apply via non-Aadhaar mode with physical document scrutiny at the RTO.","status":"PUBLISHED","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","sourceUrl":"https://sarathi.parivahan.gov.in"}],"sourceRefs":[{"title":"The Motor Vehicles (Amendment) Act, 2019","actOrRuleNumber":"Section 8 and 9","issuingAuthority":"Parliament of India / MoRTH","url":"https://morth.nic.in","status":"PUBLISHED","lastVerifiedAt":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z"}],"taskSlug":"driving-licence-learner","taskName":"Learner's Licence Application","categorySlug":"vehicles","categoryName":"Vehicles and Driving","isStateOverride":false,"stateCode":"MH","stateName":"Maharashtra","stateSlug":"maharashtra"},"relatedTasks":[{"slug":"driving-licence-new","name":"Permanent Driving Licence Application","description":"How to get a permanent driving licence in India after holding a learner pe